  "major": "Interactive Media Arts",
  "notes": "Source: Five Towns College Catalog, 2025-26 Edition v.1.2 (© 2025), official PDF at https://www.ftc.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/FTC.Catalog.2025-26.v8.-v.1.2.Final_.2026.0728.pdf . CREDENTIAL HONESTY: Five Towns College offers NO Bachelor of Science in Computer Science and NO Bachelor of Science in Computer Software in the 2025-26 catalog (verified; the 2022-23 and 2023-24 catalogs also list no computing bachelor's — bachelor's offerings are B.B.A., Mus.B., B.F.A., B.S. in Mass Communication only). Its true computing bachelor's is the B.F.A. in Interactive Media Arts (HEGIS 1009.00, program code 39171), IPEDS-classified under Computer & Information Sciences / Computer Software and Media Applications — it covers interactive computer graphics programming (HTML/CSS/JavaScript), 3D animation, motion design, and design technology. Transcribed verbatim from the catalog's official 'Recommended Sequence of Courses' (pp. ~11121-11270 of the PDF text), 8 semesters x 15 credits = 120, matching the catalog's published 'Total Program Credits: 120'. Prerequisites taken from each course's catalog description. TITLE DISCREPANCY (honest): the recommended-sequence page labels IMA 350 as 'Interactive Computer Graphics 1' (apparent typo); the official course description titles it 'Interactive Computer Graphics 3' with prerequisite IMA 250, used here. Choice slots (SCI/MAT/SOC/ART/ELECT/LAS/IMA electives) use choice:true with placeholder codes since the catalog leaves the specific course to the student. elective credit 'Elective (1/2/3)' slots: program table lists 9 total elective credits. No 0-credit required courses; no external placement/assessment prerequisites beyond catalog listings.",
